					<description><![CDATA[<p>AI Infrastructure Expansion Gains Investor Support Australian artificial intelligence infrastructure company Firmus raised $2 billion through new equity funding for regional expansion initiatives. The investment will accelerate development of large-scale</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/firmus-raises-2b-ai-infrastructure-funding/" data-wpel-link="internal">Firmus Raises $2B To Expand AI Infrastructure Across Asia-Pacific</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h2><b>AI Infrastructure Expansion Gains Investor Support</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Australian artificial intelligence infrastructure company Firmus raised $2 billion through new equity funding for regional expansion initiatives. The investment will accelerate development of large-scale artificial intelligence computing facilities across Australia and Asia-Pacific markets.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Existing investors Coatue and Nvidia participated alongside new investors supporting the company&#8217;s latest funding round successfully. Blackstone Tactical Opportunities, additional Blackstone investment vehicles, and Jane Street also committed capital to Firmus successfully.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The latest financing values Firmus at more than $10.5 billion post-money. It nearly doubles the company&#8217;s valuation from its April funding round and increases total equity raised over the past year to more than $3 billion.</span></p>
<h2><b>Funding Accelerates AI Factory Rollout</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Firmus will use fresh capital expanding Project Southgate, providing artificial intelligence training and inference infrastructure capabilities. The company also plans to begin early development of its recently announced artificial intelligence infrastructure project in Indonesia.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Firmus has established manufacturing capabilities in Australia for its proprietary HyperCube platform. The infrastructure is built on Nvidia&#8217;s DSX AI Factory Reference Architecture, enabling faster deployment of AI computing systems while improving energy efficiency and system resilience.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Co-Chief Executive Officer Oliver Curtis said the investment enables the company to advance multiple projects simultaneously as demand for AI computing infrastructure continues to rise. Firmus is preparing additional expansion across selected Asia-Pacific markets to support growing enterprise artificial intelligence demand.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Project Southgate represents a major part of Firmus&#8217; long-term expansion strategy across the region. The company aims to provide scalable computing capacity for organisations developing large AI models and enterprise applications. </span></p>
<h2><b>Strategic Partnerships Strengthen Growth Plans</b></h2>
<div id="attachment_204137" style="width: 1322px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-204137" class="size-full wp-image-204137" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Firmus-2.png" alt="Illustration of AI cloud infrastructure featuring GPU-powered data centres, strategic technology partnerships, and institutional investment driving enterprise AI expansion." width="1312" height="736" /><p id="caption-attachment-204137" class="wp-caption-text">Strategic partnerships between AI infrastructure providers, technology leaders, and institutional investors are accelerating cloud expansion to meet growing enterprise demand for high-performance AI computing. Source: Created by Ventureburn.</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The investment further expands Firmus&#8217; relationship with Nvidia after both companies signed a strategic agreement in June. Under that partnership, Firmus purchases Nvidia infrastructure while providing cloud services powered by the chipmaker&#8217;s technology.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Blackstone&#8217;s participation introduces another major institutional investor as global investment firms continue increasing exposure to AI infrastructure projects. Existing investor Coatue also expanded its position during the latest financing round.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">By combining our proprietary technology, localized manufacturing, and repeatable deployment process, Firmus is ideally placed to serve the increasing demand we’re seeing from both enterprise customers and AI-native organizations in our region. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Also, Jane Street participated in the financing round, which demonstrates the increasing investor trust in companies delivering physical AI infrastructure. It’s also smart to invest now in infrastructure expansion since AI adoption will drive up customer demand over time.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">More News: </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/omilia-secures-67m-series-b-funding/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">Omilia Secures $67M To Expand AI Customer Experience Platform</span></a></p>
<h2><b>AI Infrastructure Becomes A Strategic Investment Focus</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Demand for AI infrastructure continues to grow as enterprises require greater computing capacity for training and deploying advanced </span><a href="https://cloud.google.com/discover/what-is-an-ai-model" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">AI models</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400">. Enterprise and government organisations continue driving demand for advanced artificial intelligence infrastructure across Asia-Pacific markets rapidly.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Former cryptocurrency mining companies have increasingly shifted towards AI infrastructure by repurposing data centres, power assets and high-performance computing facilities. The trend reflects growing demand for long-term infrastructure that supports large-scale AI workloads.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Firmus said Australia will remain the primary destination for most of the newly raised capital while regional expansion progresses gradually. The company believes its existing manufacturing capabilities and software platform provide a strong foundation for deploying additional AI infrastructure before expanding further across Asia-Pacific markets.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The financing highlights continued investor confidence in artificial intelligence infrastructure despite wider concerns about sector spending. Firmus believes the investment strengthens its position as demand for artificial intelligence computing capacity continues increasing.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">To stay updated on crypto venture capital funding and market trends, visit our </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/category/news/venture-capital/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">venture capital news section</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> for more insights.</span></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/firmus-raises-2b-ai-infrastructure-funding/" data-wpel-link="internal">Firmus Raises $2B To Expand AI Infrastructure Across Asia-Pacific</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
