					<description><![CDATA[<p>Funding Accelerates AI-Powered Virtual Care Expansion  HealthSnap secured $25 million to beef up its balance sheet and grow its AI virtual care platform. The HealthSnap money will be used for</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/healthsnap-secures-25-million-growth-financing/" data-wpel-link="internal">HealthSnap Secures $25M To Expand AI-Powered Virtual Care Platform</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h2><b>Funding Accelerates AI-Powered Virtual Care Expansion </b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">HealthSnap secured $25 million to beef up its balance sheet and grow its AI virtual care platform. The HealthSnap money will be used for investment in its AI platform, Commercial, and Customer Success </span><a href="https://www.stratsimple.com/glossary/initiative/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">initiatives</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> on a national level. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The money will be used for product development and commercial growth and to grow its Advanced Primary Care offering. HealthSnap plans broader deployment across leading United States health systems, strengthening virtual care adoption nationwide.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The financing was led by Eastward Capital Partners. Alongside refinancing existing debt, the facility provides additional capital to advance artificial intelligence capabilities and expand enterprise adoption of the company&#8217;s healthcare platform.</span></p>
<h2><b>AI Investment Accelerates Virtual Care Expansion</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company recently launched its AI-enhanced Advanced Primary Care Management solution, combining agentic AI with clinical workflows to help healthcare teams manage larger patient populations more efficiently.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Its platform integrates Remote Patient Monitoring, Chronic Care Management, Principal Care Management, Advanced Primary Care Management, enterprise analytics, reimbursement optimisation, and care coordination into a single electronic medical record-integrated system.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Chief Executive Officer and co-founder Samson Magid said the funding validates HealthSnap&#8217;s long-term vision of making continuous, intelligent healthcare the standard across modern health systems. He added that artificial intelligence is designed to strengthen clinical teams rather than replace healthcare professionals.</span></p>
<h2><b>Platform Growth Strengthens Healthcare Delivery</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">HealthSnap has experienced rapid growth as healthcare providers increasingly adopt AI-driven care management solutions. Its platform processes two patient measurements every second while reducing clinical alert frequency by 97% for patients after their first year of enrolment.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company currently supports more than 80,000 active patient programmes across 200 health systems and physician organisations. HealthSnap expects supporting more than 100,000 active care programmes by the end of 2026 successfully worldwide.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The business partners are Prisma Health, AdventHealth, Ascension Health and Sentara Health which are in different locations in the USA. Furthermore, partners such as Tampa General Hospital, UnityPoint Health, Baptist Health South Florida and Mount Sinai Medical Center.</span></p>
<h2><b>Artificial Intelligence Improves Clinical Efficiency<br />
</b></h2>
<div id="attachment_204106" style="width: 1322px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-204106" class="size-full wp-image-204106" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/a-futuristic-poster-glows-with-vibrant-n_x9r1BTC-UMefcVAC2zHbxA_NkAhBBxCQMuSdxHse9fCEA.png" alt="A neon futuristic visual showing AI assisting healthcare professionals with patient data and virtual care." width="1312" height="736" /><p id="caption-attachment-204106" class="wp-caption-text">HealthSnap uses AI to enhance clinical decision-making and streamline virtual healthcare delivery. Source: Created by Ventureburn</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The majority of every point of HealthSnap&#8217;s care delivery can now be assisted by artificial intelligence. Through 2025 the company&#8217;s AI platform assessed over three million clinical progress notes, going far beyond manual audits to facilitate greater quality assurance.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">AI-simulated patient interactions are also enabling newly hired nurses to practice interacting with patients, which the company states is contributing to a Net Promoter Score of 72 while simultaneously enabling better employee and patient engagement.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The platform also generates clinical summaries which can streamline disparate patient information to allow for quicker, more educated clinical decisions. AI agents also help with patient enrollment, device support, and compliance outreach. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">More News: </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/aurelius-systems-raises-40m-to-advance-autonomous-defense-platform/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">Aurelius Systems Raises $40M To Advance Autonomous Defense Platform</span></a></p>
<h2><b>Funding Supports Long-Term Healthcare Innovation</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">During three years, HealthSnap has achieved an increased revenue over fivefold and steady year-over-year business growth. It achieved the 2025 MedTech Breakthrough honorable mention for both clinical workflow and operational proficiency.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Driven by successful organic business development, HealthSnap has solidified its position as a rapidly expanding player in the healthcare landscape and was identified as one of the fastest-growing American companies in the Inc. 5000 listing for 2025. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The investment proceeds will also provide the impetus to further expand its teams of artificial intelligence specialists, engineers, and product developers and fuel company growth into both existing and new healthcare enterprises around the world.</span></p>
